This licence covers only the work added to this container by the FaMAF CVA6
Project. Every path below is a path inside the container:

  - scripts/               the run drivers, the sweep, the cleaner, the VCD
                           window tool and the viewer server
  - CVA6_configs/          the configuration package the sweeps read
  - benchmarks/config/     the calibration programs, written for the gem5
                           comparison
  - benchmarks/viewer/     the teaching programs written for the viewer
  - CVA6Flow/              the CVA6Flow viewer and its tracer, offered under
                           this same MIT licence in its own repository at
                           https://github.com/FaMAF-CVA6-Project/CVA6Flow
  - README.md              the documentation written for this container

  - verilator_changes/     PARTLY, and only the modifications. Both files in
                           custom_size_vcds/, ariane_tb.cpp and the Makefile,
                           are modified copies of files belonging to the OpenHW
                           Group and ETH Zurich. The changes made to them are
                           this project's. The files themselves stay under
                           their original Apache 2.0 and Solderpad 0.51 terms,
                           and each carries a notice saying what was changed,
                           as those licences require. The unmodified originals
                           are at corev_apu/tb/ariane_tb.cpp and the Makefile
                           at the root of this container.

It does not cover the CVA6 core, its SoC wrapper, the verification harness or
the vendored dependencies. Those are the work of the OpenHW Group and
contributors and stay under their original licences, preserved in this container
as LICENSE, LICENSE.Berkeley and LICENSE.SiFive.

It does not cover the toolchain under tools/ either. The RISC-V GNU toolchain,
Verilator and Spike are built into the image from their own sources and stay
under their own terms.

